\section{What remains open and how to resume}

The main completed computational consequence is Theorem~\ref{thm:population}, including its binary-horizon, shared-quantile sampler, bounded-denominator, and robust-regularity deductions. Its proof does not defer an analytic lemma or import a cutpoint oracle. Its practical limits are the configuration graph's growth with automaton size, denominator, and accuracy, and the mandatory linear cost of printing a full long word. Independent originality and external mathematical validation remain unknown. An exact threshold decision, exact finite-horizon attainment algorithm, or polynomial dependence on all input parameters has not been established.

The quantum continuation proves the sharp global replication horizon and an operational rigidity/classicality theorem. Acquisition of the measurement and dictionary, calibrated implementation costs, and a major unresolved quantum/computational consequence remain exact gaps. The uniform dimension-free marginal-broadcasting recovery route is already disproved. The separable infinite-dimensional extension is preserved separately pending root reconstruction and does not inherit a finite record or ancilla budget.

The fixed-order overlapping-block extension now has an explicit integral filler and compiled sampler, with its denominator-squared cost charged in Section~\ref{sec:blocks}. A hard next representation question is whether that extra denominator dependence can be removed, or whether a genuinely conditional stochastic-kernel interface admits a comparable completion. General junction-tree gluing beyond the word-chain interface is preserved separately from the completed chain theorem. General Gaussian radial profiles, a stronger source-conditioning characterization for transport, and the finite-precision compiler derived from OpenAI family 139 remain independently scoped open or conditional routes. Its exact-real sampling theorem is an imported premise, not a theorem certified by this investigation.

For continuation, start with Section~\ref{sec:population} and \texttt{proofs/finite\_population\_compiler.txt}, then the executable exact-rational solver and its model/certificate receipts. The hard next problem is a substantive stronger information interface or improved dimensional complexity, rather than further demonstrations of the same graph. Sections~\ref{sec:replication}
